WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.556
"The Beast of the Otherworld?" Zann echoed. "What's that?"

2
00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:07.450
He didn't recognize the creature from his parents' books.

3
00:00:07.451 --> 00:00:11.302
And he was sure he'd remember something that looked like that

4
00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:16.405
! "It's the most horrible beast in all the worlds." Wyssa

5
00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:22.355
shuddered. "How was Morb able to transport it from its home on

6
00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:27.975
Narakan?" "Narakan?" Venna sounded startled. "I thought that world was only a

7
00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:37.935
myth." "Apparently not," Wyssa said. The creature hissed, and a dark, viscous substance dripped from its jaws and sizzled on the stone

8
00:00:37.936 --> 00:00:44.334
bridge. "How big is that thing, anyway?" Perda cried as the enormous head rose even

9
00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:49.828
higher. "Big!" Zann answered. "And it doesn't seem to be in a good mood

10
00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:53.303
either!" The Beast let out a hoarse, echoing cry.

11
00:00:53.304 --> 00:00:57.440
Then its head snaked toward Zann and the others.

12
00:00:57.441 --> 00:01:00.152
"Run!" Venna shouted.

13
00:01:00.153 --> 00:01:09.825
The humans scattered. Zann lunged toward the gate and skidded across the rough stone on his hands and knees.

14
00:01:09.826 --> 00:01:18.088
When he glanced back, the Beast was raising its head again.

15
00:01:18.089 --> 00:01:22.520
Zann noticed that the dark goo wasn't coming from its mouth after all.

16
00:01:22.521 --> 00:01:24.758
It was oozing out of its head.

17
00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:29.311
"Look out!" Gliss screamed. "It's going to strike again!"

18
00:01:29.312 --> 00:01:33.234
Spurting angry flames, Zing flew toward the Beast.

19
00:01:33.235 --> 00:01:37.184
"Zing, no!" Zann shouted. "It's going to eat you!"

20
00:01:37.185 --> 00:01:41.415
The Beast snapped at the small dragon. Zing barely escaped.

21
00:01:41.416 --> 00:01:46.574
"We have to zap away!" Gliss cried, grabbing Darb's hand.

22
00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:51.652
"No!" Wyssa said. "That's the worst thing we can do.

23
00:01:51.653 --> 00:02:01.568
If the legends are true, the Beast can catch hold of Transport spells and pull its victims back—straight into its jaws."

24
00:02:01.569 --> 00:02:09.966
"So we're trapped?" Perda snapped her fingers, and a sword appeared in her hand. "Then we'll have to fight."

25
00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:15.005
Zann stared at her for a second. When had Perda become so brave?

26
00:02:15.006 --> 00:02:19.880
He couldn't imagine any other kid his age facing down a monster so calmly.

27
00:02:19.881 --> 00:02:22.378
But this was no time to think about such things.

28
00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:25.909
Rubbing his hands together, Zann conjured his own sword.

29
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:30.505
"Stand back, kids," Venna called. "I'm going to blast it."

30
00:02:30.506 --> 00:02:35.046
"Wait," Wyssa said. "I don't think that will—"

31
00:02:35.047 --> 00:02:36.429
Blast

32
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.517
! A bolt of energy shot out of Venna's

33
00:02:39.518 --> 00:02:44.426
hands. It flew straight at the Beast. The Beast opened its giant mouth . . .

34
00:02:44.427 --> 00:02:46.696
Gulp

35
00:02:46.697 --> 00:02:52.157
! "Did the Beast just eat the Blast spell?" Gliss

36
00:02:52.158 --> 00:02:57.182
cried. Zann didn't have time to answer as he dodged another sizzling drop of

37
00:02:57.183 --> 00:03:01.526
slime. He found himself beside Darb, who was still cradling the

38
00:03:01.527 --> 00:03:05.214
mibbit. "The mibbit doesn't seem too worried," Zann

39
00:03:05.215 --> 00:03:11.425
commented. Darb nodded. "Vee told us the effects of the ear-rubbing would last a few hours, remember?" he

40
00:03:11.426 --> 00:03:16.011
said. "Too bad. I bet the mibbit was the only thing holding the Beast back

41
00:03:16.012 --> 00:03:23.854
before." "You're probably right. No wonder the mibbit was tense with that thing around." Zann glanced up. "Get

42
00:03:23.855 --> 00:03:26.850
back!" He and Darb leaped away in opposite

43
00:03:26.851 --> 00:03:31.081
directions. The Beast's head slammed down, shaking the whole

44
00:03:31.082 --> 00:03:34.990
bridge. "Hurry! Run while it's stunned!" Perda

45
00:03:34.991 --> 00:03:38.681
shouted. "Maybe it won't be able to climb out of that pit and chase

46
00:03:38.682 --> 00:03:46.302
us." Zann sprinted for the gate. He was only halfway there when a shimmering wall of magic energy shot up in front of

47
00:03:46.303 --> 00:03:48.245
him. "What's that?" Venna

48
00:03:48.246 --> 00:03:53.821
cried. Zann didn't answer. He lowered his head and ran straight toward the magical

49
00:03:53.822 --> 00:03:56.721
wall. But he bounced off it and stumbled into

50
00:03:56.722 --> 00:04:02.289
Darb. "Oof," Darb grunted. He fell backward, almost slipping off the edge of the

51
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.327
bridge. To catch himself, he had to drop the

52
00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:10.901
mibbit. The fuzzy creature landed on its feet and just stood there, flicking its ears

53
00:04:10.902 --> 00:04:16.077
lazily. "Look out!" Perda yelled. "The Beast is coming for you guys!"

54
00:04:16.078 --> 00:04:19.595
Zann grabbed Darb and dragged him away from the Beast.

55
00:04:19.596 --> 00:04:27.239
The Beast's orange eyes glowed, and another wall of magic energy sprang up inside the first.

56
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:35.149
"Why did it make another wall? The first one seemed to be working pretty well." Zann winced, touching his shoulder.

57
00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:40.012
He would definitely have a bruise to heal later— if he survived

58
00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:43.390
this. "I think it's herding us back toward

59
00:04:43.391 --> 00:04:49.222
itself." Suddenly Perda looked scared. "Look! It's

60
00:04:49.223 --> 00:04:54.346
drooling." "This is hopeless!" Gliss cried, her voice

61
00:04:54.347 --> 00:04:59.630
shaking. "The Beast is going to eat us, and there's nothing we can do about

62
00:04:59.631 --> 00:05:05.108
it!" Darb grabbed the mibbit. "Isn't there anything you can do?" he asked Wyssa and

63
00:05:05.109 --> 00:05:14.053
Venna. Wyssa was peering at the magic walls. "Let me think, let me think," she muttered. "There must be a way . .

64
00:05:14.054 --> 00:05:16.729
." Zann glanced from Wyssa to his

65
00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:20.319
friends. Perda and Gliss were clinging to each other, looking

66
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:26.752
terrified. Zing was hiding behind Venna. Darb, cradling the mibbit, was looking nervously at the

67
00:05:26.753 --> 00:05:31.948
Beast. The hideous creature was sizing them up, as if deciding whom to eat

68
00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:37.722
first. Suddenly Zann's eyes lit up. "I've got it! Everyone run toward the

69
00:05:37.723 --> 00:05:40.940
tower!" "What?" Venna said. "Are you

70
00:05:40.941 --> 00:05:45.003
crazy?" Zann didn't answer; he raced along the bridge toward the

71
00:05:45.004 --> 00:05:49.873
tower. Perda caught up to him. "Zann, the door is bolted

72
00:05:49.874 --> 00:05:56.480
shut! And we won't have time to try to open it with a spell. The Beast will have us cornered!"

73
00:05:56.481 --> 00:06:03.079
"Just go." Zann shoved her forward and then turned to make sure the others were following.

74
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:07.738
Wyssa was the last to run past. She gave Zann a strange look.

75
00:06:07.739 --> 00:06:10.960
"I hope you know what you're doing, boy."

76
00:06:10.961 --> 00:06:17.840
Zann hoped so too. He glanced at the Beast, which was already gathering itself for another attack.

77
00:06:17.841 --> 00:06:22.907
As the huge head snaked toward him, Zann sprinted after the others.

78
00:06:22.908 --> 00:06:26.385
He could feel the creature's hot breath on the back of his neck.

79
00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:32.263
A drop of viscous goo landed on his shoulder, burning right through his shirt.

80
00:06:32.264 --> 00:06:43.378
Zann yelped in pain. He picked up speed, trying not to imagine the Beast's sharp teeth digging into his skin.

